📌 What is a List in Python? (Simple Definition)

A list is a container that stores multiple values in one variable.

Instead of creating many variables like this:

a = 10
b = 20
c = 30


You can store all of them together in one list:

numbers = [10, 20, 30]
-----
🧠 Think of a List Like…
📦 A box with compartments

Each box can hold:

numbers

words

or even other lists

example:
items = ["apple", "banana", "mango"]
-----


✏️ Lists are Mutable (Beginner-friendly meaning)

Mutable means you can change the list after creating it.

Example:

numbers = [1, 2, 3]
numbers[1] = 10
print(numbers)

Output:

[1, 10, 3]

🧠 One-Line Summary (Remember This)

A list is an ordered, changeable collection of values stored in one variable.